  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "Honest notes",
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "\n- **Light traffic result:** sharing raised GPU busy from about 12% to 68% and doubled latency (85 ms to 177-197 ms mean, p95 99 ms to about 330 ms). Mean shown is the average of the six pods.\n- **Heavy load result:** six copies delivered about 5x less total throughput than one copy, because one tiny server already fills the card. Sharing helps when many models each get light traffic, not when one model is saturated.\n- **Equal speed:** utilization, throughput and training time did not differ between the two paths. Do not read the first-time setup bar as a Kubernetes win: it is the one-time cost.\n- **Recovery times** are from pod logs and polling (about +/- 3 s). Not tested: Growing, Moving, MIG, the Operator installing the driver or toolkit.\n- Source: `results-ubuntu-4070.md` in the repo, branch `ubuntu-4070`.\n"
   },
